                        <field name="dc_description">Consists of three seperate pamphlets scanned together under an unrelated cover page for the pamphlet "Report of the debate in the House of Commons of Ireland on Friday the 14th of February, 1800 : on the subject of a legislative union with Great Britain : containing the speeches of ... Messrs. Ponsonby, Lord Castlereagh, Egan ... and the reply of Henry Grattan, esq. : also the petitions from the county of Carlow ...". -- Printed by J. Milliken, 32, and J. Rice, 111 Grafton Street, Dublin.  Pamphlet no. 1 entitled "Parliamentary register, or, History of the proceedings and debates of the House of Commons of Ireland : which met at Dublin on ... the 18th [i.e. 15th] January, 1800. Part the first". -- Printed for John Milliken, 32 Grafton Street, Dublin. -- "Part the first on Sir Laurence Parsons amendment on the address to His Majesty".  Pamphlet no. 2 entitled "Debates, Wednesday, 5th February, 1800". -- No publisher listed; [s.n.]. -- No author listed.  Pamphlet no. 3 entitled "A report of the debate in the House of Commons of Ireland on Wednesday and Thursday the 5th and 6th of February, 1800 : on the King's message recommending a legislative union with Great Britain containing the propositions : also petitions from the city and county of Dublin ...". -- Printed by J. Milliken, 32, and, J. Rice, 111 Grafton Street, Dublin. </field>
